Regarding differences between menstrual cycle and oestrous cycle:<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong><span style="white-space:nowrap;">Statement I:</span></strong></td><td>Animals that have oestrous cycles resorb the endometrium if conception does not occur during that cycle and animals that have menstrual cycles shed the endometrium through menstruation instead.</td></tr><tr><td><strong><span style="white-space:nowrap;">Statement II:</span></strong></td><td>&nbsp;In species with oestrous cycles, females are generally only sexually active during the oestrus phase of their cycle and females of species with menstrual cycles can be sexually active at any time in their cycle, even when they are not about to ovulate.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Statement I is correct, Statement II is incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Statement I is correct, Statement II is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Statement I is incorrect, Statement II is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Statement I is incorrect, Statement II is incorrect.</td></tr></tbody></table>
